{"book":"PSA","chapter":123,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3,4],"records":[{"id":"PSA.123.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"שִׁ֗יר הַֽמַּ֫עֲל֥וֹתאֵ֭לֶיךָ נָשָׂ֣אתִי אֶת־עֵינַ֑י הַ֝יֹּשְׁבִ֗י בַּשָּׁמָֽיִם׃","gloss":"The song of the ascents. To you I have lifted up my eyes, the [one] sitting in the heavens.","pieces":[[1,"A song of ascents. I raise my eyes to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}, the one who reigns in heaven.",null]],"L":{"1":"A song of ascents. To {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} I lift up my eyes, [the one] sitting in the heavens."},"R":{"1":"A song for the journey up to Jerusalem. I look up to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}. You sit on {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} throne in heaven."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"punctuation","tokens":["o191230010011","o191230010021","o191230010022"],"choice":"The title shares verse 1","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 120:1, the short title and the first line are counted together as verse 1, so the verse numbers are the same as in Bibles that print the title without a number.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191230010011","o191230010022"],"choice":"a song of ascents: probably a pilgrim song","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 120:1: one of the fifteen songs probably sung by pilgrims going up to Jerusalem.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191230010072"],"choice":"sitting: sitting enthroned","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (yashav) used of God means sitting as king on his throne (2:4; 29:10).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o191230010041"],"choice":"I have lifted up: I lift up now","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb is in the form often used for past events, but here it describes what the psalmist is doing now.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191230010011","o191230010022"],"choice":"A song for the journey up to Jerusalem","alternatives":["A song of ascents"],"reason":"As in 120:1.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191230010072"],"choice":"reigns (B); sit on your throne (R)","alternatives":["sit"],"reason":"Balanced and Readable say what God's sitting means (m3).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":"Eyes on {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, like a servant's on a master","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.123.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"הִנֵּ֨ה כְעֵינֵ֪י עֲבָדִ֡ים אֶל־יַ֤ד אֲֽדוֹנֵיהֶ֗ם כְּעֵינֵ֣י שִׁפְחָה֮ אֶל־יַ֪ד גְּבִ֫רְתָּ֥הּ כֵּ֣ן עֵ֭ינֵינוּ אֶל־יְהוָ֣ה אֱלֹהֵ֑ינוּ עַ֝֗ד שֶׁיְּחָנֵּֽנוּ׃","gloss":"Look, as [the] eyes of slaves to [the] hand of their masters, as [the] eyes of a female slave to [the] hand of her mistress, so our eyes [are] to YHWH our God until that he shows us favor.","pieces":[[2,"Servants watch the hand of their master, and a servant woman watches the hand of the woman she serves. In the same way we keep our eyes on {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} our God, waiting for {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} to show us favor.",null]],"L":{"2":"Look, as the eyes of slaves [are] to the hand of their masters, as the eyes of a female slave [are] to the hand of her mistress, so our eyes [are] to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} our God until {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} shows us favor."},"R":{"2":"Servants keep watching their master's hand to see what he wants or what he will give. A servant woman watches the hand of the woman she works for. In the same way, we keep looking to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} our God. We wait for {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} to be kind to us."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191230020051","o191230020101"],"choice":"the hand of their master: signal and gift","alternatives":["the hand that punishes","the hand that protects"],"reason":"Slaves watched the master's hand for a sign of what was wanted, for the food and wages it handed out, and for help. The picture is of complete attention and dependence.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191230020182"],"choice":"show favor: be gracious","alternatives":["have mercy"],"reason":"The verb (chanan) means to show undeserved kindness to someone in need. It is repeated twice in verse 3.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o191230020061"],"choice":"masters: plural of majesty or each one's master","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word for \"their master\" is plural in form, as it often is for a master or lord; it may also mean each slave's own master.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o191230020051"],"choice":"to see what he wants or what he will give","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable explains why the servants watch the hand (m1).","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191230020031","o191230020081"],"choice":"servants; servant woman","alternatives":["slaves; slave woman"],"reason":"\"Servant\" in Balanced and Readable, as the style guide has it; the meaning decision (m1) keeps that these are slaves watching a master, and Literal keeps \"slaves\" and \"female slave\".","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.123.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"חָנֵּ֣נוּ יְהוָ֣ה חָנֵּ֑נוּ כִּֽי־רַ֝֗ב שָׂבַ֥עְנוּ בֽוּז׃","gloss":"Show us favor, YHWH, show us favor, for much we have been filled [with] contempt.","pieces":[[3,"Show us favor, {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, show us favor, for we have swallowed more contempt than we can bear.",null]],"L":{"3":"Show us favor, {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, show us favor, for we have been greatly filled [with] contempt."},"R":{"3":"{{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, be kind to us! Be kind to us! People have looked down on us more than we can stand."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o191230030061"],"choice":"filled with contempt: had too much of it","alternatives":[],"reason":"To be \"filled\" or \"sated\" with something is to have had more than enough of it. Here the people have been made to swallow contempt until they can take no more.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191230030071"],"choice":"contempt: being despised","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (buz) is scorn shown to people treated as worthless (Nehemiah 3:36 has the same complaint).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191230030071"],"choice":"People have looked down on us","alternatives":["contempt"],"reason":"Readable says who showed contempt and what it was.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.123.4.s1","verses":[4],"source":"רַבַּת֮ שָֽׂבְעָה־לָּ֪הּ נַ֫פְשֵׁ֥נוּ הַלַּ֥עַג הַשַּׁאֲנַנִּ֑ים הַ֝בּ֗וּז לִגְאֵ֥יוֹנִֽים׃","gloss":"Much has it been filled for itself, our soul, [with] the mockery of the ones at ease, the contempt of the proud.","pieces":[[4,"We have had our fill and more of the mockery of the comfortable and the contempt of the arrogant.",null]],"L":{"4":"Our soul has been greatly filled for itself [with] the mockery of those at ease, the contempt of the proud."},"R":{"4":"We are tired of being mocked by people with easy lives, and of being looked down on by proud people."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191230040062"],"choice":"those at ease: the complacent","alternatives":["the secure","the careless"],"reason":"The word (sha'anan) means untroubled and secure. Here it describes people comfortable enough to look down on others (Amos 6:1; Isaiah 32:9).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o191230040011","o191230040021"],"choice":"much ... filled: repeated from verse 3","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verse takes up the end of verse 3, \"much ... filled\", and says what the contempt was and who showed it.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191230040041","o191230040042"],"choice":"our soul (L); we (B, R)","alternatives":["my soul"],"reason":"As in Psalms 1-12, nefesh is \"soul\" at Literal; Balanced and Readable say \"me\" or \"my life\", since the word means the whole living person.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o191230010011","text":"שִׁ֗יר","after":" ","lemma":"שִׁיר","morph":"Ncbsc","gloss":"the.song","strong":"7892","transliteration":"šiyr","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine or feminine singular construct (of ...)"},{"id":"o191230010021","text":"הַֽ","after":"","lemma":"הַ","morph":"Td","gloss":"of","strong":"1886a","transliteration":"ha","lang":"H","parse":"Particle · definite article"},{"id":"o191230010022","text":"מַּ֫עֲל֥וֹת","after":"","lemma":"מַעֲלָה","morph":"Ncfpa","gloss":"the.ascents","strong":"4609","transliteration":"mmaʿălôṯ","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · feminine plural absolute"},{"id":"o191230010031","text":"אֵ֭לֶי","after":"","lemma":"אֶל","morph":"R","gloss":"to","strong":"0413","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o191230010032","text":"ךָ","after":" ","lemma":"הוּא","morph":"Sp2ms","gloss":"you","strong":"3509b","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Suffix · pronoun · 2nd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o1912300